=== Human CO_Mega model (human liver) ===

[1] Computing codon frequencies from CDS sequences...
  Loaded 19,229 genes from /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/general/sequence_CDS/human/tables/human_CDS_sequences_MANE_Select_ensembl.csv
  19,229 of 19,229 genes have an Ensembl gene ID (native to the MANE GTF).
  Dropped 1 genes with missing/unusable CDS sequences (not a multiple of 3, or too short); 19,228 genes remain.
  18,351 autosomal (chr 1-22) genes, 834 X-linked genes, 43 Y-linked genes.
  Saved codon frequencies to /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/tables/human/codon_frequencies_human_liver.csv

[2] Loading human liver TE data...
  [key uniqueness] all_human_genes_merged_data.csv (TE_FILE): 12,086 rows, 12,086 distinct 'ensembl_gene_id' values; 0 values are duplicated (covering 0 rows).
  12,092 genes with TE_mean (6 Y-linked, from /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_riboseq/tables/human_liver/chromosome_te_analysis_Y.csv).
  [join audit] human codon frequencies (CDS, Ensembl gene ID) (19,228 rows, key='ensembl_gene_id') x human TE (Ensembl gene ID) (12,092 rows, key='ensembl_gene_id'):
    duplicated keys: 0 in human codon frequencies (CDS, Ensembl gene ID), 0 in human TE (Ensembl gene ID)
    unmatched: 7,208 human codon frequencies (CDS, Ensembl gene ID) keys with no match in human TE (Ensembl gene ID); 72 human TE (Ensembl gene ID) keys with no match in human codon frequencies (CDS, Ensembl gene ID)
    rows after merge ('inner'): 12,020
    Saved unmatched-key audit (7,280 rows) to /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/tables/human/join_audit_codon_vs_te_train_human_liver.csv
  12,020 genes with both codon frequencies and TE_mean.

[3] Fitting TE_mean ~ codon frequencies on autosomal genes...
  Training on 11,613 autosomal genes, 61 codon predictors.
  R^2 = 0.5385   Adjusted R^2 = 0.5360   n = 11613
  Saved intercept + 61 codon coefficients to /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/tables/human/co_mega_model_coefficients_human_liver.csv
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/human/co_mega_regression_fit_train_human_liver.png  (Pearson R = 0.7338, Pearson R² = 0.5385, p = 3.388e-1952, n = 11,613)
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/human/co_mega_regression_fit_train_spearman_human_liver.png  (Spearman rho = 0.7500, Spearman rho² = 0.5625, p = 4.464e-2087, n = 11,613)

[3b] Regression diagnostics (linearity, homoscedasticity, normality)...
  --- Regression diagnostics (autosomal training genes, Human liver) ---
  Normality of TE (actual, log2 scale, n=11,613): skew = 0.073, excess kurtosis = 0.257, D'Agostino K^2 p = 1.61e-08, Jarque-Bera p = 6.62e-10
  Normality of residuals: skew = -0.475, excess kurtosis = 1.084, D'Agostino K^2 p = 2.04e-141, Jarque-Bera p = 5.21e-219
  Homoscedasticity (Breusch-Pagan): LM stat = 265.924, p = 2.14e-27
  Linearity (Ramsey RESET, power=3 on fitted values): F = 102.713, p = 6.09e-45
  (in each test, p < 0.05 => reject the null of normality / homoscedasticity / linearity)
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/human/co_mega_regression_diagnostics_te_histogram_human_liver.png
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/human/co_mega_regression_diagnostics_residual_histogram_human_liver.png
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/human/co_mega_regression_diagnostics_residual_qq_human_liver.png
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/human/co_mega_regression_diagnostics_residual_vs_fitted_human_liver.png
  Saved diagnostic statistics to /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/tables/human/co_mega_regression_diagnostics_stats_human_liver.csv

